Codex App DeepSeek Gateway

This repository contains an independent integration for the official Codex App.
The integration code is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

It depends on pure protocol modules from codex-deepseek-runtime at
cb788738864e97a16cde82f3c584164162ab6f7c (published 0.6.7, Apache-2.0).

The current native patches modify OpenAI Codex source at
720fec862a608ae1e5878d1eecb04fb93192e93c (Apache-2.0).
Historical N/J producer records refer separately to Codex commit
680c4ba93ec79c292287fb9e0b627dc7a76e3b5e; they are not the current O165 build.
Upstream LICENSE and NOTICE are retained in licenses/.
Modified source identities and patch provenance are recorded in native/.

Native producer attribution clarification
-----------------------------------------
The retained licenses/codex-NOTICE is the exact NOTICE from the immutable O165
producer source identified by fingerprint
370c680b6dbaa093cd36afab2db2c2f821b0c54b3bdecef76e1f951e8ac02289.
Its statement that both ACL coordination modules were reused "without source
changes" was draft wording. The final acl_lock.rs derives from CDS 0.6.7 and
adds a read-only pinned-parent accessor and a root metadata-handle
classification assertion. Its hash is
149b498cba58b6b6984e96b1719e9dfd232aacabe5b968c9b01474233194bedb.
The private_acl_lock.rs module remains byte-identical to the CDS producer,
with hash b83c9c39f03115b98279e35eeb1c5cd422bc4632e087a44e83b2391c5f3d9581.
The additions do not replace ACE policy, introduce a new lock protocol, or
implement an agent, tool, approval or thread scheduler. Exact modified-file
identities and patches accompany the native distribution. This clarification
does not alter the retained producer source or its original build identity.

The proprietary desktop App package is obtained separately from its official
publisher; it is not included in this source repository or Python package.
Additional binary dependencies require their corresponding license notices
in any assembled native distribution.

The build-time native notice collector follows the CDS collector; it does not
load CDS runtime code. Canonical SPDX license texts retain the source commit,
URLs and checksums recorded in native/license-data.json. Native distributions
retain each external crate's declared license and original available notices.
